\name{summaries}
\alias{summaries}
\alias{summarise_pva}
\alias{summarise_trajectory}
\alias{summarise_accounting}
\title{Viability, trajectory and accounting summaries}
\usage{
summarise_pva(
  result,
  metric = "n_alive",
  threshold = 1,
  process_name = NULL,
  include_initial = NULL,
  occurrence = NULL
)

summarise_trajectory(
  result,
  metric = "n_alive",
  threshold = 1,
  process_name = NULL,
  include_initial = NULL,
  occurrence = NULL
)

summarise_accounting(result)
}
\arguments{
\item{result}{A \code{pva_run} from \code{\link{run_scenario}} (or its census data frame). \code{summarise_accounting()} also accepts the result of \code{\link{execute_processes}} or a bare accounting data frame.}
\item{metric}{Name of the census metric to summarise.}
\item{threshold}{Quasi-extinction threshold: a run is below threshold when \code{metric < threshold}.}
\item{process_name}{Select the interval census by name when more than one is recorded.}
\item{include_initial}{Whether year zero counts. The default includes it when the scenario supplies an initial census.}
\item{occurrence}{Select the scheduled occurrence (1, 2, ...) when the same census name appears several times.}
}
\description{
\code{summarise_pva()} reports the probability of being below the threshold at the horizon, the probability of ever falling below it (first crossing), time to threshold and final abundance, each with a Monte Carlo standard error or interval. \code{summarise_trajectory()} gives the same quantities by year. \code{summarise_accounting()} reconciles every interval by cohort.
}
\details{
Proportions carry a binomial Monte Carlo standard error and a 95 percent Wilson interval. The restricted mean time to threshold counts runs that never cross as reaching the horizon. Year \code{t} is the census taken in interval \code{t - 1}; year 0 is the initial census. Both risk functions apply the same year-zero and census selection. Passing the whole run checks every scheduled run and interval, including extinct replicates. A bare census table only identifies runs and times present in that table.

\code{summarise_accounting()} checks \code{n_start + births + introductions - deaths - removals = n_end} for each run and interval and reports losses separately for residents, individuals born in the interval and individuals introduced in the interval.
}
\value{
\code{summarise_pva()} returns a one-row data frame, \code{summarise_trajectory()} one row per year, and \code{summarise_accounting()} one row per run and interval with a logical \code{reconciled}.
}
